---
import StandardLifecycleNotice from "../../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import StandardPageLayout from "../../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../../data/standards/hgb/drs15.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  subtitle={metadata.nativeTitle}
  framework="hgb"
  status={metadata.status}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Part of the DRS consolidation wave" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Why withdrawn" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Status summary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <StandardLifecycleNotice
    type="withdrawn"
    explanation="This standard has been withdrawn."
    targetStatus="Replaced by DRS 20"
    link="/germany/drs/drs20"
    linkText="View DRS 20"
  />

  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Part of the DRS consolidation wave</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card warn">
<div class="ctitle">Part of the DRS consolidation wave</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 15 was, alongside DRS 5 (risk reporting), the DRSC's original general standard elaborating the Konzernlagebericht content requirements under §315 HGB, established in detail in the earlier HGB poster series. Its companion, DRS 15a, addressed specifically the takeover-law disclosures required for listed parent AGs (paralleling §315a HGB's own takeover-related disclosure content, also documented in that earlier poster) — the "Übernahmerelevante Angaben" this whole HGB series flagged when covering §289a/§315a.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Why withdrawn — the centrepiece of the entire DRS management-report consolidation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card info">
<div class="ctitle">Why withdrawn — the centrepiece of the entire DRS management-report consolidation</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 15 and DRS 15a, together with DRS 5 (risk reporting) and its own sector variants, were ALL folded into the single, comprehensive DRS 20 "Konzernlagebericht" — the genuine centrepiece of this entire consolidation wave. Rather than requiring practitioners to cross-reference several separate, narrower standards to understand the full Konzernlagebericht requirements, DRS 20 consolidates business review, forecast, risk, opportunity, internal control, and takeover-related disclosure content into one unified document, adopted 14 September 2012.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Status summary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card">
<div class="ctitle">Status summary</div>
<div class="td-table">
<div class="th"><span>Field</span><span>Detail</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Original topics</span><span>General management report content (DRS 15); takeover-law disclosures (DRS 15a)</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Successor</span><span><strong>DRS 20 — Konzernlagebericht</strong> (the current, active, comprehensive standard — see the DRS 20 poster for full detail)</span></div>
</div>
</div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
